92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Silicone offers a unique combination of properties not found together in other substances. Its molecular structure provides great flexibility and elastic recovery, allowing it to bend, stretch, compress, and rebound without cracking or losing form, which is ideal for applications requiring dynamic movement. It also demonstrates reliable thermal stability across a wide temperature range, remaining flexible at low temperatures without becoming overly soft at high temperatures. Furthermore, silicone can be formulated for biocompatibility, meeting standards such as cytotoxicity, which makes it a trusted material for skin-contact applications in consumer wearables and medical devices.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
