/P 81 0 R
/E (Beyond the established methods, new approaches are in development, aiming to solve remaining challenges. One interesting concept is gel-supported printing, shown by the new Rapid Liquid Print Levity system. This method proposes printing silicone directly inside a tank of a supportive gel. The gel holds the liquid silicone in place as it is deposited, eliminating the need for traditional support structures and potentially allowing for faster printing of large, flexible objects.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Approaches using highly specialized systems are emerging for fields like medicine. The Prayasta Silimac P250 is a printer designed specifically for manufacturing patient-specific soft-tissue implants and prostheses. It incorporates features like an in-built UV sterilization for print chamber and contamination-free support system, addressing the cleanliness requirements of implant manufacturing. It also has real-time curing using IR laser & heaters, increasing the time efficiency of the print. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
